      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SAVE ME GARY (5) hit the ground running last time with a strong early split and tried to lead throughout but had to settle for the minors when second (23.61) at Horsham over 410m. The form out of his last race has been franked. Can measure up this time. COLLECTIVE KAOS (1) hit the ground running and set it up early clocking 22.31 with a 1.75 lengths win at this track over 390m. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card in scoring last start. Should feature again. PAW JAXSON (8) showed little early speed at his last couple, the latest finishing sixth (22.76) in a Grade 5 H at Geelong. Solid record at the distance winning two races. Should be in this for a long way. BUSH JEWEL (2) missed the placings here last start but is well-placed to atone.",
